WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.330
When a flood takes the towers down,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.480
your phone still works.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.052
The network doesn't.

00:00:08.437 --> 00:00:11.107
A spoken sentence is heavy:

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:14.407
two hundred and fifty-six kilobits a second,

00:00:14.457 --> 00:00:15.257
as raw audio.

00:00:15.597 --> 00:00:17.967
But the links that survive a disaster,

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.887
Bluetooth, a crowded hotspot,

00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:23.878
a long-range radio, carry only a few hundred bits.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.240
So iTantra doesn't send your voice.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.794
It sends what you said.

00:00:30.284 --> 00:00:33.144
Speech becomes text on your phone.

00:00:33.194 --> 00:00:35.434
A few dozen bytes cross the link.

00:00:35.484 --> 00:00:37.814
And the other phone speaks it aloud,

00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:39.690
in ten Indian languages.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.160
Everything runs on the phone itself.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.043
No cloud. No internet.

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:50.643
Open speech models from I I Sc,

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:53.633
I I T Madras and AI4Bharat listen,

00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.103
and speak, in Hindi,

00:00:56.153 --> 00:00:57.554
Tamil, Bengali and seven more.

00:00:58.937 --> 00:00:59.807
If there's no Wi-Fi,

00:00:59.857 --> 00:01:01.517
it finds Wi-Fi Direct.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:05.487
Then Bluetooth. And the same packets are ready for

00:01:05.537 --> 00:01:07.048
a LoRa radio bridge.

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:12.267
Each sentence packs into a compact binary frame,

00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:14.057
a median of sixty-two bytes,

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.816
encrypted and signed once phones are paired.

00:01:18.393 --> 00:01:21.053
Alerts cut through at full volume.

00:01:21.103 --> 00:01:22.753
And one tap sends an SOS,

00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:25.459
with your location, read aloud on the other side.

00:01:28.537 --> 00:01:29.937
On a real phone,

00:01:29.987 --> 00:01:33.727
recognition runs twenty times faster than speech,

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:36.361
and idle CPU stays under two percent.

00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:41.157
iTantra. Speak in your language,

00:01:41.207 --> 00:01:45.474
and be heard, even when the towers go silent.

00:01:45.954 --> 00:01:49.534
Smart India Hackathon twenty twenty-six.

00:01:49.584 --> 00:01:52.630
ISRO problem statement two six one seven three.
